Question -------------  Table: Employee

+-------------+---------+
| Column Name | Type    |
+-------------+---------+
| id          | int     |
| name        | varchar |
| salary      | int     |
| managerId   | int     |
+-------------+---------+
id is the primary key (column with unique values) for this table.
Each row of this table indicates the ID of an employee, their name, salary, and the ID of their manager.
 

Write a solution to find the employees who earn more than their managers.

Return the result table in any order.

The result format is in the following example.

 

Example 1:

Input: 
Employee table:
+----+-------+--------+-----------+
| id | name  | salary | managerId |
+----+-------+--------+-----------+
| 1  | Joe   | 70000  | 3         |
| 2  | Henry | 80000  | 4         |
| 3  | Sam   | 60000  | Null      |
| 4  | Max   | 90000  | Null      |
+----+-------+--------+-----------+
Output: 
+----------+
| Employee |
+----------+
| Joe      |
+----------+
Explanation: Joe is the only employee who earns more than his manager.








Solution --------------   select e.name as employee 
                          from employee e 
                          join employee m on e.managerid = m.id 
                          where e.salary > m.salary ;





Explanation ----------------   So Here The Question Is Asking Us To Find The Employees Who Earns More Than Thier Managers . So In Order To This First We Need To 
                               To Select The Names Of Employee Because In Our Output We Need To Have The Output Wherein I Have A Coloumn With The Names Of Employee 
                               Who Earns More Than Their Managers From The Employee Table Which We Name As "e" So Write The Query Like [ select e.name as employee
                               from employee e ] . Now We Join The Employee Table With Itself Using The Join Function & We Join It On The Basis Of Managerid Bcz
                               Its Common Which Links Employee & Manager . So We Write The Query As [ join employee m on e.managerid = m.id ] For This Part . Now 
                               We Write Our Condition Which The Questions Asks Which Is Where The Employees Salary Is More Than Thier Manger's Salary So For This 
                               We Write Our Query As [ where e.salary > m.salary ] And Hence We Get Our Output Wherein We Have Joe As The Only Employee Who Earns More 
                               Than His Manager . 
